summary: This file sets up two programs.

[program:reports-export] program="reports-export"
  summary: Runs a shell command and waits for you to start it.
  1 section [program:reports-export]
    => Starts a program section. Visor and supervisorctl call it reports-export.
  2 key     command=sh -c ': visor-sandbox; while :; do sleep 5; done'
    => What it runs: a shell command.
  3 key     stopasgroup=true
    => When you stop it, the stop signal also goes to everything it started, so nothing is left behind.
  4 key     killasgroup=true
    => If it has to be killed, its child processes are killed too.
  5 key     autostart=false
    => Doesn’t start with supervisord. It runs only when you start it.
  6 key     stdout_logfile=/var/log/supervisor/reports-export.log
    => Its output goes to this file. supervisord writes it, and the Logs tab reads it.
  6 unset   not set: autorestart, stderr_logfile
    => Defaults apply: it’s restarted only if it exits with an unexpected code and its errors go to a file supervisord names itself.
    suggest: Its errors go to a file supervisord names itself. It’s hard to find and is deleted when supervisord restarts.
    add: stderr_logfile=/var/log/supervisor/reports-export.err.log

[program:reports-sync] program="reports-sync"
  summary: Runs the program at /nonexistent/sync and starts with supervisord.
  8 section [program:reports-sync]
    => Starts a program section. Visor and supervisorctl call it reports-sync.
  9 key     command=/nonexistent/sync
    => What it runs: the program at /nonexistent/sync.
 10 key     stopasgroup=true
    => When you stop it, the stop signal also goes to everything it started, so nothing is left behind.
 11 key     killasgroup=true
    => If it has to be killed, its child processes are killed too.
 11 unset   not set: autostart, autorestart, stdout_logfile, stderr_logfile
    => Defaults apply: it starts with supervisord, it’s restarted only if it exits with an unexpected code and its output and errors go to files supervisord names itself.
    suggest: Files supervisord names itself are hard to find and are deleted when supervisord restarts. Set both log paths.
